<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/li-shi-cheng-han"><span class="enc-name">Li Shi (Cheng-Han)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Li Shi was the last ruler of Cheng-Han, the Sixteen Kingdoms state in Sichuan, reigning from 343 to 347.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/li-shiji"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/li-shiji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Li Shiji</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Li Shiji, often called Li Ji, was one of the leading generals of the early Tang dynasty in China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/li-shou"><span class="enc-name">Li Shou</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Li Shou was emperor of Cheng-Han in Sichuan from 338 to 343.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/li-si"><span class="enc-name">Li Si</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Li Si was a Legalist statesman, chancellor to Qin Shi Huang, the First Emperor of China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/li-te"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/li-te.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Li Te</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Li Te was a Ba-Di leader who led refugees fleeing famine in the north-west into Sichuan around 298, under the Western Jin dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/li-thai"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/li-thai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Li Thai</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Li Thai, who reigned as Maha Thammaracha I, was king of Sukhothai from about 1347 to 1368.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/en